description:
benches/session_and_urls.rs:259-270 (bench_websocket_capability_deserialize):

    fn bench_websocket_capability_deserialize(c: &mut Criterion) {
        let raw = typical_session_json();
        let session: Session = serde_json::from_str(raw).expect('typical session must parse');
        c.bench_function('session_websocket_capability_deserialize', |b| {
            b.iter(|| {
                let cap = session
                    .websocket_capability()
                    .expect('ws capability must parse');
                black_box(cap);
            })
        });
    }

The output is wrapped in black_box, but the INPUT session is not. The other six benchmarks in the same file (e.g. bench_primary_account_id_hit at line 248, bench_session_deserialize_typical at 171) consistently black_box BOTH ends of the iteration.

In practice the optimizer is unlikely to constant-fold this case because session.websocket_capability re-runs serde_json::from_value on a serde_json::Value (which allocates per call). Low practical risk.

But the divergence makes the bench harder to reason about. A future maintainer comparing the seven benches would see six consistent shapes and one anomaly, and either (a) waste time wondering whether the omission is intentional, or (b) copy-paste a new bench from the anomaly without thinking, propagating the inconsistency.

Fix: wrap session in black_box at line 264:
    let cap = black_box(&session)
        .websocket_capability()
        .expect('ws capability must parse');
